#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# finite_field_primitive_element

#% text
# `finite_field_primitive_element(F)` gives the primitive element of the finite field `F` with the least index.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A primitive element generates the multiplicative group: its powers are all the nonzero elements.

#% item
# The generator `x` of a field with a Conway polynomial is primitive, but an element of smaller index may be too.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
finite_field_primitive_element(finite_field(7, 2))
#% output
#= finite_field_element(finite_field(7, &(3 + 6*&1 + &1^2), "Polynomial"), [0, 1])

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A prime field, a field with the exponential representation and an extension:

#% cell
[finite_field_primitive_element(finite_field(2, 1)), finite_field_primitive_element(finite_field(7, 2, "Exponential")), finite_field_primitive_element(finite_field(11, 3))]
#% output
#= [finite_field_element(finite_field(2, &(1 + &1), "Polynomial"), [1]), finite_field_element(finite_field(7, &(3 + 6*&1 + &1^2), "Exponential"), 2), finite_field_element(finite_field(11, &(9 + 2*&1 + &1^3), "Polynomial"), [0, 1])]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Over a prime field it is the least primitive root:

#% cell
[finite_field_primitive_element(finite_field(23, 1)), primitive_root(23)]
#% output
#= [finite_field_element(finite_field(23, &(18 + &1), "Polynomial"), [5]), 5]

#% text
# The element is primitive, and no element of smaller index is:

#% cell
Q = finite_field(7, 2)
p = finite_field_primitive_element(Q)
[is_finite_field_element_primitive(p), finite_field_index(p), map(k => is_finite_field_element_primitive(Q(k)), range(1, finite_field_index(p) - 1))]
#% output
#= [true, 7, [false, false, false, false, false, false]]

#% text
# The norm of a primitive element is a primitive root of the prime field:

#% cell
[finite_field_element_norm(finite_field_primitive_element(finite_field(11, 3))), primitive_root(11)]
#% output
#= [2, 2]

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# The argument must be a field; anything else stays unevaluated:

#% cell
finite_field_primitive_element(5)
#% output
#= finite_field_primitive_element(5)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_finite_field_element_primitive`, `primitive_root`, `finite_field_log`
